# Secrets — NEVER COMMIT

Every value this product needs at runtime lives here, and nowhere else. This file is **git-ignored**: it stays on this computer and never reaches GitHub. The assistant reads it and derives `.env` from it. Only the **names** ever appear in code.

**How the values get here: you write them here yourself.** The assistant tells you which line to fill in and where to obtain the value; you open this file in the editor, paste it on the right line, and save. **Never paste a credential into the chat** — this file is the place for it, and it is the only place.

The real file is `secrets/secrets.local.md`, next to this one. It already exists as a blank form; if it ever goes missing, copy this template over it.

```
# --- the product's own secrets ---
SECRET_KEY=

# --- generated by the assistant and handed back to you ---
ADMIN_USER=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# --- messenger / login bot (Bale or Eitaa), if the product uses one ---
# BALE_BOT_TOKEN=
# EITAA_TOKEN=

# --- other API keys this product needs (the assistant adds the names here) ---
# <SERVICE>_API_KEY=

# --- the server, filled in at /deploy (default path only) ---
# SERVER_IP=
# SERVER_USER=
# SERVER_PASSWORD=
# DOMAIN=
```
